      "path": "src/coordinators/trade-workflows/record-position-change.ts",
      "content": "This checks the stored lifecycle projection rather than the lifecycle derived from effective facts. If an otherwise coherent Open trade has a stale `Closed` projection, every position change now returns `TradeClosed` before analysis can report and repair the disagreement, breaking the existing P7 repair path. Derive the before-state first, preserve `IntegrityDisagreement` for incoherent facts, and use its `expectedLifecycle` for this guard. Add a regression case with open facts and a stored `Closed` lifecycle.",
      "existing_code": "  if (prepared.before!.lifecycle === 'Closed') return rejected(deps, [{ source: 'TradeWorkflows', code: 'TradeClosed' }]);",
      "start_line": 336,
      "end_line": 336,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/coordinators/trade-workflows/record-position-change.ts",
      "content": "These findings are not necessarily caused by the command: `derive` also returns path findings from `candidate.before`. If the existing facts already oversell or go flat before later facts, this converts that integrity failure into a normal `Rejected` quantity issue, bypassing `IntegrityDisagreement`. Derive/check the before-state first and preserve its integrity failures; only translate path failures introduced by the candidate into P22 command issues.",
      "existing_code": "  if (derived?.kind === 'IncoherentFacts') {\n    issues.push(...positionPathIssues(derived.findings, positionChange.versions[0]!.value.memberIds));\n  }",
